WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:06.671
"Do Low Level Laser Therapy Devices
Work for Hair Loss?"

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.060
In my book, How Not to Age,

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.000
I discuss all the drugs,
foods, supplements,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:14.580
and surgeries that can treat
age-related hair loss,

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.340
but what about non-dietary,
non-drug,

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.020
non-surgical interventions?

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.560
Autologous platelet-rich plasma,

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.960
where concentrated portions
of your own blood

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.660
is repeatedly injected
into your scalp,

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.320
appears to have an efficacy
similar to the available drugs,

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.160
though the available evidence
is considered insufficient

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.740
to recommend it,
and so remains unapproved

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.980
in the U.S. or Europe
for hair restoration purposes.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.040
Scalp Botox
is also not recommended.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:46.980
The thought was
that relaxing scalp muscles

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.180
might improve blood flow,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.280
but when actually put
to the test

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:51.900
actually caused hair loss

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:53.340
in some pilot study
participants.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:57.360
Then, there are lasers.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.040
In the 1960s,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.960
a Hungarian physician
published the paper,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.860
"The effect of laser beams
on the growth of hair in mice,"

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.860
detailing
a serendipitous discovery

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.980
that a low-powered ruby laser
increased the hair growth

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:12.900
on the shaved backs of mice.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.320
The mechanism appears to be
increased blood flow.

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:19.380
The floodgates opened
when the FDA cleared

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.360
the first low-level
laser therapy device

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.240
for age-related
pattern hair loss in 2007,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.060
and now, there are clinics
advertising lasers

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.680
for everything
from tennis elbow

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:31.140
to "scrotal rejuvenation."

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:35.160
There have been at least ten
randomized, controlled trials

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.140
of low-level
laser therapy devices

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:40.320
for hair loss, and the efficacy
has been found comparable

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.300
or even superior to the drugs.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.180
They are noninvasive and appear
to be relatively safe.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.880
Mild side effects
include itching, acne,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:48.900
and scalp tenderness

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.120
that usually resolves
within two weeks.

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:54.180
Reviews typically conclude
that laser therapy

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.300
may be a promising alternative
to drugs and scalpels,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:00.660
but there remains
considerable skepticism

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.340
within the dermatology community

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:03.960
and for good reason.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:06.900
Most of the laser therapy trials

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.760
were funded
by the manufacturers

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.380
of the tested products
themselves.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.380
This is true of hair loss
treatments across the board,

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:17.160
but laser studies appear
particularly reticent

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:20.940
to provide visual evidence
or inquire

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:23.280
about perhaps the most important
outcome of all,

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:24.600
patient satisfaction.

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.560
When the first independent study
was performed,

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:31.440
blinded evaluations
of before-and-after photographs

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.100
could not detect a difference
in hair density or caliber.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:38.280
In two studies that compared
subjective satisfaction

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.620
between laser
and sham placebo devices,

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:43.200
no significant difference
could be found either.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.140
In other words,
from the patient's perspective,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.300
they just plain don't work.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.920
So, while there are

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:52.500
statistically significant
improvements

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:53.940
in hair density and thickness,

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:57.720
there may be little clinically
significant improvement.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.200
If you want to give them
a try anyway,

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.780
there are at least 29
FDA-cleared devices

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:04.740
currently on the market.

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:08.100
There have been no head-to-head
studies between them,

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:09.960
but based on measured outcomes,

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:11.640
there appear to be
no difference

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:14.640
between the comb-style
and hat-style devices,

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:17.940
though those containing
laser diodes exclusively

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:19.260
may have an edge over devices

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:22.260
that include a mix
of both laser diodes and LED.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:25.200
Do not look into the light,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.320
as prolonged retinal exposure
could be damaging.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.260
Thankfully,
at least most cap designs

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.880
have a built-in safety shut-off

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.680
to avoid accidental
eye exposure.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.100
Otherwise,
besides general safety caveats

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.960
about using
electrical contraptions

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:40.920
in or around water,

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:43.020
such devices are
considered safe,

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.360
though they are contraindicated

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.520
for those with cancer
of the scalp

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.160
due to the potential
for stimulatory effects.

